WEBVTT

00:00.850 --> 00:06.190
Drawn by a landscape as white as snow,

00:00.850 --> 00:06.190
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

00:06.240 --> 00:12.740
I'm headed toward an unseen world.

00:06.240 --> 00:12.740
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

00:18.460 --> 00:21.680
I've been traveling while lost

00:18.460 --> 00:21.680
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

00:21.710 --> 00:24.470
Under this gray sky.

00:21.710 --> 00:24.460
Nezumiiro no sora no shita

00:24.500 --> 00:30.560
Every day with new maps, stained with my many dreams.

00:24.500 --> 00:30.560
Higawari no chizu ikutsumo no yume ga nijindeita

00:30.560 --> 00:32.950
I wonder if someday,

00:30.560 --> 00:32.950
Itsuka wa sa

00:32.970 --> 00:36.990
Even with these tiny steps of mine,

00:32.970 --> 00:36.990
Chippoke na boku no kono hohaba demo

00:37.010 --> 00:43.070
I'll be able to travel beyond those clouds.

00:37.010 --> 00:43.070
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

00:43.070 --> 00:44.700
I put on a bold front.

00:43.070 --> 00:44.700
Tsuyogatte

00:44.700 --> 00:46.250
End up hurting myself.

00:44.700 --> 00:46.250
Kizutsuita

00:46.280 --> 00:49.330
I feel empty inside.

00:46.280 --> 00:49.330
Kokoro sukashita youni

00:49.330 --> 00:50.870
It's started to rain,

00:49.330 --> 00:50.870
Furidashita

00:50.870 --> 00:53.040
And the raindrops

00:50.870 --> 00:53.040
Amatsubu tachi ga

00:53.040 --> 00:56.260
Began to repeat their scattered reflections.

00:53.040 --> 00:56.260
Ranhansha kurikaesu

00:56.280 --> 00:59.130
These straight rays of light

00:56.280 --> 00:59.130
Massugu na hikari ga

00:59.130 --> 01:01.850
Start to cross one another.

00:59.130 --> 01:01.850
Kousa shite

01:01.880 --> 01:05.430
And without telling anyone where they're headed,

01:01.880 --> 01:05.430
Yakusaki mo tsugenumama

01:05.430 --> 01:06.720
Across the endless distances,

01:05.430 --> 01:06.720
Doko made mo

01:06.720 --> 01:08.310
They pass through all matter.

01:06.720 --> 01:08.310
Tsukinukeru

01:08.330 --> 01:14.140
I burn these faint afterimages onto my eyes.

01:08.330 --> 01:14.140
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakitsukete

01:14.140 --> 01:16.060
Under this sky,

01:14.140 --> 01:16.060
Kono sora no shita

01:16.060 --> 01:19.890
Wherever I am,

01:16.060 --> 01:19.890
Donna toko ni itemo

01:20.310 --> 01:22.190
I should be able to reach

01:20.310 --> 01:22.190
Todoku hazu nanda

01:22.190 --> 01:27.000
The unseen world.

01:22.190 --> 01:27.000
Mada minu sekai e

01:42.390 --> 01:45.810
This is the bullet used in the murder of Brigadier General Hughes.

01:46.600 --> 01:50.730
.45 caliber, and only one shot was fired.

01:50.730 --> 01:54.190
I'd like to say the murderer was skilled, but it was a close proximity shot.

01:54.740 --> 01:57.200
Not impossible for a woman to do.

02:00.160 --> 02:02.830
What is the caliber of your gun?

02:03.620 --> 02:05.460
.45.

02:06.790 --> 02:10.090
This is your ammunition request application.

02:10.090 --> 02:11.670
Am I right?

02:14.550 --> 02:16.840
It's written here you only needed to be supplied with one shot.

02:16.840 --> 02:18.470
What did you use it for?

02:19.260 --> 02:21.220
As it says right there,

02:21.600 --> 02:25.100
I used it at Research Laboratory 5, while I escorted Edward Elric...

02:27.980 --> 02:32.190
But Research Laboratory 5 is closed down, and there shouldn't be anyone there.

02:32.190 --> 02:33.980
But there were.

02:33.980 --> 02:36.490
...According to you.

02:38.490 --> 02:41.740
Should I order a search for this bullet you supposedly shot?

02:42.240 --> 02:46.910
Research Laboratory 5 is in ruins now due to an unknown explosion.

02:48.040 --> 02:52.920
So the place where you say you used
your gun is usually unvisited by people,

02:52.920 --> 02:57.010
and even if we wanted to search for
the bullet, it'd be under a heap of rubble...

03:00.220 --> 03:06.680
There's witness testimony stating you left the scene of the crime, on the exact date and time it occurred.

03:06.680 --> 03:07.980
That's ridiculous!

03:08.390 --> 03:09.980
Compose yourself.

03:10.600 --> 03:13.230
What were you doing at the time?

03:14.230 --> 03:17.820
I was on leave that day and at my parents' house.

03:18.110 --> 03:20.490
You can confirm with them.

03:21.280 --> 03:26.580
Testimony from family members or people whom you are close with cannot be accepted as an alibi.

03:29.210 --> 03:31.670
Second Lieutenant Maria Ross is currently being interrogated.

03:32.420 --> 03:34.710
Though you may be her superior, I cannot allow you to see her.

03:35.130 --> 03:36.170
I see...

03:40.550 --> 03:42.180
Major Armstrong!

03:43.050 --> 03:44.600
Sergeant Brosh.

03:45.140 --> 03:46.680
You were here, too, Major?

03:46.680 --> 03:49.600
Yeah. Are you here for Second Lieutenant Ross?

03:49.600 --> 03:50.890
Yes. The truth is-

03:52.100 --> 03:59.570
The truth is, like the lieutenant, I also fired one round at Research Laboratory 5 while escorting the Elric Brothers.

03:59.570 --> 04:00.490
What?

04:00.490 --> 04:04.240
I reported that, but they didn't listen at all.

04:06.540 --> 04:09.790
So they're planning on passing her off as the murderer?

04:16.500 --> 04:19.500
Cold Flame

04:16.500 --> 04:19.500
Cold Flame

04:23.470 --> 04:26.310
Now that I look closely, you're really scratched up.

04:27.350 --> 04:29.180
Not an easy journey, huh?

04:34.900 --> 04:37.190
Say, what are you going to do now?

04:40.860 --> 04:41.700
Hey...

04:48.040 --> 04:49.790
I wonder...

04:51.750 --> 04:53.920
Mama, don't cry.

05:02.930 --> 05:04.130
What do you want me to do?

05:08.060 --> 05:09.350
What?

05:10.060 --> 05:14.900
No, it's just that you've never asked me for advice about something concerning yourselves...

05:17.150 --> 05:18.270
Oh...

05:24.360 --> 05:25.910
It really scares me.

05:27.370 --> 05:33.330
Both of you are fighting in a place so dangerous that Mr. Hughes was killed.

05:34.290 --> 05:37.210
I got really scared when I thought about that.

05:41.590 --> 05:44.090
Because... you both could die.

05:45.050 --> 05:47.590
And suddenly disappear from my side.

05:49.680 --> 05:51.350
Just like Mom and Dad...

05:55.020 --> 05:58.440
I got really scared when I thought about that.

05:59.440 --> 06:02.400
To be honest, I want you to end your journey.

06:06.320 --> 06:08.570
I want you two to get your bodies back.

06:09.320 --> 06:11.410
But I don't want you to go on any dangerous journeys.

06:12.490 --> 06:13.290
Because...

06:15.620 --> 06:16.460
But...

06:21.840 --> 06:22.750
Sorry.

06:24.420 --> 06:28.220
I don't really know what I want either.

06:31.100 --> 06:32.720
You're really kind, Winry.

06:32.720 --> 06:35.140
Huh?! W-W-What are you saying?

06:35.140 --> 06:37.980
I'm always kind!

06:37.230 --> 06:40.270
Stop! You're going to scratch me up even more!

06:37.980 --> 06:38.440
PLACEHOLDER

06:38.440 --> 06:41.360
Geez Al, what are you saying?

06:46.860 --> 06:48.030
There.

06:49.740 --> 06:51.530
Evening paper!

06:52.080 --> 06:52.950
Finally!

06:53.410 --> 06:55.700
What, the paper again?

06:55.700 --> 06:58.170
I'm forced to watch over you all day.

06:58.870 --> 07:01.210
This is about the only thing I can look forward to.

07:05.920 --> 07:08.550
Warrant Officer Falman speaking. I'm calling from an outside line.

07:08.550 --> 07:10.510
Please put me through to Colonel Mustang.

07:11.350 --> 07:12.970
That's right. My code is...

07:12.970 --> 07:15.180
What's the deal?

07:15.180 --> 07:18.940
Airam, George, Oliver, 4649.

07:20.650 --> 07:23.690
It's that lady from back then!

07:26.690 --> 07:28.200
Philosopher's stones...

07:29.360 --> 07:32.200
Ones who have tattoos of Ouroboros...

07:33.580 --> 07:35.080
Homunculus...

07:37.580 --> 07:38.620
How are they...

07:38.620 --> 07:39.500
Brother!

07:40.870 --> 07:41.830
Look at this...

07:41.830 --> 07:44.000
Don't scare me like that.

07:44.000 --> 07:46.710
I... got this from the front desk!

07:47.880 --> 07:49.380
What is it?

07:52.050 --> 07:53.550
What?!

07:54.350 --> 07:58.980
"Second Lieutenant Maria Ross convicted on charges of the murder of Brigadier General Hughes"?!

08:01.810 --> 08:03.270
I don't believe this.

08:03.270 --> 08:06.360
Maybe the colonel or the major might know something.

08:06.360 --> 08:07.820
Aren't you going to tell Winry?

08:08.360 --> 08:09.780
I'll explain it to her later.

08:13.410 --> 08:15.370
I don't like this thing.

08:15.370 --> 08:18.830
Quit complaining. It's kind of like a collar for a dog.

08:19.160 --> 08:20.910
Oh, and I'm going to ask again just to be sure...

08:20.910 --> 08:23.170
Are you really fifteen?

08:23.170 --> 08:24.670
Yeah.

08:24.670 --> 08:26.040
Stop lying.

08:26.040 --> 08:28.420
But it's true...

08:30.510 --> 08:31.420
What's all this?

08:32.380 --> 08:33.340
What's going on?

08:33.340 --> 08:34.470
An intruder!

08:34.470 --> 08:35.760
Please lend us a hand!

08:35.760 --> 08:36.680
What?!

08:37.220 --> 08:38.680
You'd better behave!

08:38.680 --> 08:39.430
Yes, sir!

08:42.770 --> 08:45.060
Weak, weak, weak!

08:45.060 --> 08:47.690
Are you guys even trying?!

08:48.280 --> 08:49.570
What's with this guy?!

08:49.570 --> 08:51.070
Guns aren't working at all!

08:52.570 --> 08:53.320
Move!

08:53.320 --> 08:53.950
You-

08:55.990 --> 08:56.660
Whoa!

09:06.540 --> 09:10.010
But it's awfully boring not being allowed to cut them.

09:10.510 --> 09:13.090
Hello! Guy who's not affected by guns!

09:13.090 --> 09:15.140
Could you let me out of here?

09:15.140 --> 09:16.760
Who are you?

09:16.760 --> 09:18.890
An illegal alien from Xing.

09:18.890 --> 09:20.220
Oh, I see.

09:20.220 --> 09:22.730
Must have been a long trip.

09:22.730 --> 09:24.600
I'll help you if you let me out!

09:24.600 --> 09:27.110
I don't have time to mess around with you...

09:29.360 --> 09:31.030
What country did you say you're from?

09:31.030 --> 09:32.610
Xing of the East.

09:34.530 --> 09:35.740
Come with me.

09:35.740 --> 09:36.910
Thanks.

09:45.210 --> 09:46.330
What?

09:53.720 --> 09:55.880
Hello, Honey!

09:55.880 --> 09:57.760
I've finally found you!

09:58.680 --> 10:00.310
You were at Research Laboratory 5-

10:01.260 --> 10:04.230
I'm glad you remember me.

10:04.810 --> 10:10.360
I think of you every time I see the hole in my right hand you shot through.

10:10.360 --> 10:13.320
Ms. Murderer of Hughes.

10:13.650 --> 10:15.150
That's a misunderstanding!

10:15.150 --> 10:16.530
Is it really?

10:16.530 --> 10:20.030
The paper says it's confirmed.

10:20.030 --> 10:21.160
No way...

10:21.580 --> 10:26.750
At this rate, it looks like you're going to have the guilt pinned on you and get executed by a firing squad.

10:26.750 --> 10:27.540
You're kidding...

10:28.250 --> 10:30.500
There's no way... If they investigate thoroughly-

10:31.250 --> 10:32.750
Make a decision!

10:32.750 --> 10:36.760
Get tortured to death by these guys or escape with me!

10:36.760 --> 10:38.090
Those are the two choices you've got!

10:41.180 --> 10:42.390
That's horrible...

10:43.180 --> 10:45.730
Are those the only choices available?

10:45.730 --> 10:47.390
Looks that way.

10:50.650 --> 10:52.270
God, damn it!

10:52.270 --> 10:55.570
Mom, Dad, I'm sorry!

10:58.240 --> 11:01.280
Fine, I'll escape. Happy?

11:01.280 --> 11:04.450
You'd better escort me, you stupid bone armor!

11:04.450 --> 11:06.660
Wow, you've got spunk.

11:07.710 --> 11:09.500
Women have to have guts!

11:11.000 --> 11:11.710
Yes.

11:12.250 --> 11:14.250
Yes, I understand.

11:17.630 --> 11:19.630
Notify the entire city.

11:19.630 --> 11:21.140
Maria Ross has escaped from jail.

11:21.640 --> 11:25.270
She's with a fiendish partner. Capture her immediately.

11:25.770 --> 11:27.020
If she resists...

11:27.930 --> 11:30.060
...don't hesitate to kill her!

11:36.110 --> 11:37.440
How much longer are we going to run?!

11:38.190 --> 11:39.360
Shut up and keep running!

11:42.320 --> 11:43.580
Second Lieutenant Ross?!

11:44.160 --> 11:46.490
Edward! Alphonse!

11:48.750 --> 11:50.670
Hey! You're that guy from-

11:51.080 --> 11:52.210
And Ling, too?!

11:52.210 --> 11:53.170
Hiya!

11:53.170 --> 11:54.710
What are you guys up to?

11:54.210 --> 11:55.800
That's what we should be asking!

11:57.420 --> 11:58.550
We don't have much time!

12:00.090 --> 12:01.220
You...

12:01.640 --> 12:05.220
Lady, go straight down that alley to reach the warehouse district!

12:05.220 --> 12:07.220
It's dark enough over there to make your escape!

12:07.220 --> 12:10.100
Second Lieutenant Ross, about Lt. Colonel Hughes...

12:10.100 --> 12:13.190
Hurry up! If the military police finds you, they'll shoot you dead!

12:13.900 --> 12:15.020
Second Lieutenant Ross!

12:15.020 --> 12:16.270
Don't follow her!

12:16.270 --> 12:17.400
Second Lieutenant!

12:17.400 --> 12:19.190
Second Lieutenant Ross!

12:34.330 --> 12:36.540
You're Maria Ross, right?

12:43.550 --> 12:44.760
What?!

12:44.760 --> 12:46.550
Oh, so she did it?

12:46.550 --> 12:47.510
Hey!

12:47.510 --> 12:48.720
Hold it!

12:50.020 --> 12:51.690
Whoa!

12:51.890 --> 12:53.600
We're going, thin-eyes!

12:53.600 --> 12:54.730
You got it!

12:55.150 --> 12:57.730
Ling! Why are you working with a guy like that?!

12:57.730 --> 12:59.480
We'll talk later!

13:01.030 --> 13:02.490
Seriously...

13:09.790 --> 13:11.500
Yo, Fullmetal.

13:17.630 --> 13:19.000
What's the meaning of this...

13:19.920 --> 13:22.630
What's the meaning of this, Colonel?!

13:40.190 --> 13:41.530
Why...

13:43.450 --> 13:45.030
Lt. Colonel Hughes was...

13:46.110 --> 13:48.030
Why would Second Lieutenant Ross...

13:48.410 --> 13:49.830
Why didn't you tell me in the first place?!

13:56.080 --> 13:58.080
Attacking a superior?

13:58.540 --> 14:00.250
Know your place!

14:09.760 --> 14:11.180
You can't, Brother!

14:11.180 --> 14:12.180
Let go of me, Al!

14:12.180 --> 14:13.560
No!

14:13.560 --> 14:15.980
This bastard just killed Second Lieutenant Ross!

14:15.980 --> 14:16.770
Second Lieutenant Ross?

14:21.070 --> 14:23.440
What is this, Colonel?!

14:24.820 --> 14:28.490
There was a kill-on-sight order issued for Maria Ross, an escaped convict.

14:29.820 --> 14:30.740
That's all there is to it.

14:30.740 --> 14:32.370
"That's all"?!

14:32.370 --> 14:35.960
I do apologize for hiding Hughes' death.

14:37.210 --> 14:41.250
But do not object to orders. Do not seek explanation.

14:42.090 --> 14:43.250
Simply obey.

14:43.880 --> 14:45.510
That's what it means to be a soldier!

14:56.100 --> 14:57.770
Colonel Mustang.

14:58.600 --> 15:01.230
Explain the situation to me.

15:02.900 --> 15:06.610
There should have been a notice issued saying if she resists, we could gun her down.

15:07.400 --> 15:09.530
She resisted, so I killed her.

15:11.700 --> 15:14.490
The Brigadier General was a good friend of yours from what I hear.

15:15.200 --> 15:15.950
Yeah.

15:17.210 --> 15:18.410
He was a good man.

15:19.870 --> 15:24.050
It weren't your men who helped
Second Lieutenant Ross escape from jail, right?

15:24.050 --> 15:25.210
Mine?

15:25.510 --> 15:26.170
Why would I?

15:26.630 --> 15:27.420
Why?

15:28.970 --> 15:32.260
So you could burn her to death like that yourself.

15:36.060 --> 15:38.770
I'd appreciate it if you didn't make assumptions.

15:48.030 --> 15:52.530
I'm truly sorry for not telling you about Brigadier General Hughes' death.

15:55.370 --> 15:56.790
Because of me...

16:00.040 --> 16:01.710
Don't brood over it.

16:02.670 --> 16:04.420
It is not your fault.

16:06.630 --> 16:08.090
So you're all here.

16:09.010 --> 16:10.340
Dr. Nox...

16:11.340 --> 16:14.350
The damage is extensive.

16:14.350 --> 16:19.850
But from a scar on her tooth that was just narrowly left unscathed, we were able to identify her as Maria Ross.

16:20.770 --> 16:22.690
How horrible.

16:22.690 --> 16:26.320
Turning a babe like that into charcoal.

16:27.900 --> 16:31.990
You must have really had something against her, eh, Mr. Mustang?

16:35.490 --> 16:37.830
Are you satisfied you were able to avenge your friend's death?

16:42.040 --> 16:48.170
It makes me sick a hero from the Ishbal War
would go so far against a little girl.

16:53.130 --> 16:58.600
Colonel, I can't express to you how sorry I am for what my subordinate did.

16:59.810 --> 17:03.600
I had no idea Second Lieutenant Ross would murder...

17:04.350 --> 17:08.020
She's always been honest... hardworking...

17:09.610 --> 17:11.190
And thoughtful...

17:24.290 --> 17:26.830
Looks like you're exhausted, Major.

17:27.340 --> 17:28.500
Why not take a vacation?

17:30.340 --> 17:33.510
Eastern Headquarters, where I used to be stationed, was great.

17:34.550 --> 17:38.680
It lacks the bustle of large cities,
and most of all, there are so many beauties.

17:46.980 --> 17:52.490
And so, Mustang was able to avenge his best friend.

17:52.990 --> 17:55.030
And everyone lived happily ever after.

17:55.030 --> 17:57.030
You petered out.

17:57.410 --> 18:00.790
Wasn't the purpose of this mission to make the colonel behave?

18:01.790 --> 18:03.450
Who cares?

18:03.450 --> 18:05.830
The dog ate its bait.

18:07.040 --> 18:10.340
And it seems he's provoking people's antipathy.

18:10.750 --> 18:13.340
His own men may even be disgusted at him.

18:15.220 --> 18:16.220
What's this?

18:17.010 --> 18:18.470
Request for leave.

18:18.470 --> 18:19.800
At this time of the year?

18:20.350 --> 18:21.350
Is something wrong?

18:22.060 --> 18:24.430
No, it's fine. I permit it.

18:24.980 --> 18:26.270
Thank you very much.

18:41.490 --> 18:43.450
Oh, for crying out loud!

18:43.450 --> 18:46.750
Why did you leave this place?! There's no knowing what the colonel will say to me if he finds out!

18:47.170 --> 18:50.460
No one saw me coming back.

18:50.460 --> 18:52.500
That's not the problem here!

18:53.000 --> 18:59.010
You're a poor soldier that's in the hands of a vicious criminal, so it's okay.

18:59.680 --> 19:00.470
Huh?!

19:02.640 --> 19:05.310
Yo, what are you doing?

19:05.310 --> 19:06.560
Sending a signal.

19:06.560 --> 19:07.730
Signal?

19:07.730 --> 19:11.980
And besides, why did you bring back some random stranger?!

19:11.980 --> 19:14.610
Young Master! We've looked all over for you!

19:14.610 --> 19:17.030
Oh wow, that was quick.

19:17.030 --> 19:18.240
More guests.

19:23.490 --> 19:26.080
Hey Elizabeth! How are you?

19:26.080 --> 19:28.330
Thanks for calling all the time.

19:28.330 --> 19:32.210
But won't your scary aide scold you if you slack off too much?

19:32.210 --> 19:35.710
It's all right! She's on leave right now.

19:36.260 --> 19:39.300
Which is why I can call you like this.

19:40.930 --> 19:41.890
What do you think?

19:41.890 --> 19:45.770
This starts as soon as the lieutenant goes on vacation.

19:46.430 --> 19:48.350
I guess she really was...

19:48.730 --> 19:50.650
...His babysitter...

19:50.650 --> 19:52.190
That's right!

19:52.610 --> 19:55.480
I haven't had any days off since I came here.

19:55.480 --> 19:57.650
So I'm thinking about taking a holiday soon.

19:57.650 --> 20:00.660
Oh? Going somewhere?

20:00.660 --> 20:02.910
I've gotten into fishing lately.

20:04.330 --> 20:05.540
Want to come along?

20:15.920 --> 20:16.590
Yes?

20:17.300 --> 20:18.420
Who is it-

20:23.550 --> 20:26.510
Why did you do that all of a sudden, Major?!

20:27.220 --> 20:29.270
Edward Elric.

20:33.020 --> 20:33.900
Oh no.

20:33.900 --> 20:36.230
Your automail is broken.

20:36.230 --> 20:37.150
Huh?

20:37.280 --> 20:40.190
Yes. This is a serious situation.

20:40.190 --> 20:42.030
We must get it fixed right away.

20:43.160 --> 20:46.280
I'll escort you to Resembool.

20:46.280 --> 20:48.160
Well, umm...

20:48.160 --> 20:49.330
What? What?

20:49.330 --> 20:51.290
We're going back to Resembool?

20:51.290 --> 20:53.790
Al, listen to this...

20:53.790 --> 20:59.170
Alphonse Elric, you stick out too much, so stay in Central.

21:00.090 --> 21:02.220
All right! Let's make arrangements for the train ride.

21:02.220 --> 21:04.550
Let's go, Edward Elric!

21:08.510 --> 21:11.770
Can you cut it out already, Major?

21:12.140 --> 21:14.100
No can do.

21:14.100 --> 21:15.940
This is also an order.

21:17.940 --> 21:19.440
From that man...

21:21.240 --> 21:23.240
Yes, I understand.

21:24.360 --> 21:27.950
Major Armstrong and Edward Elric just got on a train.

21:28.580 --> 21:29.620
I see.

21:32.500 --> 21:34.670
Now there are no hindrances.

21:41.710 --> 21:46.090
I was able to come in contact with a witness who saw the guy who assaulted the prison.

21:46.090 --> 21:48.850
And this is what he looks like.

21:49.430 --> 21:51.350
Oh, he was alive?

21:52.270 --> 21:54.350
I wonder if he has anything to do with the Flame Colonel?

21:54.350 --> 21:55.650
Who knows?

21:55.650 --> 21:58.110
But I think we can say for sure that there is a big possibility.

21:58.110 --> 21:59.610
Where did he run off to?

22:00.570 --> 22:04.530
Well, he's speedy, and to top it off,
he's also good at hiding...

22:04.530 --> 22:06.780
So in other words, you don't know?

22:06.780 --> 22:07.820
You're so incompetent.

22:07.820 --> 22:09.910
Shut up, hag.

22:09.910 --> 22:11.410
We don't have enough people, that's why.

22:11.410 --> 22:12.500
People?

22:14.660 --> 22:16.790
He's all we need.

22:19.210 --> 22:23.170
You're up, Barry the Chopper.

22:33.330 --> 22:37.420
I don't have to act tough, right?

22:33.330 --> 22:37.420
Tsuyogaranakute iindane

22:38.670 --> 22:44.220
The scribbling someone made...

22:38.670 --> 22:44.220
Dareka ga kaitetta

22:44.220 --> 22:50.020
On the wall, of a flower is swaying.

22:44.220 --> 22:50.020
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

22:50.020 --> 22:55.600
No one knows their true selves.

22:50.020 --> 22:55.600
Jibunrashisa nante dermo wakaranaiyo

22:55.600 --> 22:57.900
Even though we both lose and gain

22:55.600 --> 22:57.900
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu de

22:57.900 --> 23:01.320
By embarking on this long, long path,

22:57.900 --> 23:01.320
Nakushitari hirottari

23:01.320 --> 23:08.990
And though there may be days loneliness strikes and makes us weep...

23:01.320 --> 23:08.990
Kyuu ni samishikunatte naichau hi mo arukedo

23:11.080 --> 23:16.500
Let's transform our tears and pains to stars.

23:11.080 --> 23:16.500
Namida mo itami mo hoshi ni kaeyou

23:16.500 --> 23:22.500
Let's light a candle to illuminate our tomorrow.

23:16.500 --> 23:22.500
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

23:22.500 --> 23:27.630
And we'll hold our small hands over the fire to create stardust,

23:22.500 --> 23:27.630
Chiisana te kazashite futari de tsukurou

23:27.630 --> 23:32.850
And an eternity that shines so brilliantly.

23:27.630 --> 23:32.850
Hoshikuzu wo tsuyoku hikaru eien wo

23:32.850 --> 23:38.230
Farewells may be unavoidable,

23:32.850 --> 23:38.230
Sayonara itsuka wa kurukamoshirenai

23:38.230 --> 23:44.150
Yet the seasons continue to change obliviously.

23:38.230 --> 23:44.150
Kisetsu wa soredemo meguri megutteku

23:44.480 --> 23:48.240
Even if I lose myself, I'll continue to walk...

23:44.480 --> 23:48.240
Chiisaku mayottemo aruiteku

23:48.240 --> 23:52.280
Walk by your side.

23:48.240 --> 23:52.280
Kimi to aruiteku

23:52.280 --> 23:56.580
That's the only thing I'd like to never change.

23:52.280 --> 23:56.580
Sore dake wa kawaranaideiyoune

24:00.140 --> 24:03.890
The whole truth lies in Xerxes.

24:04.770 --> 24:07.900
The residents left in the city that rusted away and disappeared...

24:07.900 --> 24:10.860
...wipe away the darkness within the boy.

24:11.650 --> 24:15.990
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

24:15.990 --> 24:22.000
The Arrogant Palm
 of a Small Human

24:15.990 --> 24:22.000
Episode 18, The Arrogant Palm of a Small Human.

24:22.200 --> 24:26.080
Humans, raise the signal of counterattack.
